  "difficulty_level": "H1",
  "difficulty_reason": "The theorem classifies all local Noetherian rings by the existence of a nontrivial finite punctual alteration eliminating the maximal associated prime. The proof must construct this alteration either by a torsion quotient or an integral fractional element via the determinantal trick, isolate the exceptional DVR case and prove depth-two rigidity. This structural finite-modification argument is above routine Serre-condition checking.",
